     That wouldn't make it feasible to have the current possessor
accompany the item, or have shopkeepers summon Kops.  After the Wizard
of Yendor enters play, when you leave his level with him still alive
he is retained on the "migrating monsters" list instead of saved with
the level.  That way he can come to you without the program shuffling
a lot of data to and from disk.  There is already a "migrating objects"
list as well, although it doesn't know how to restore something to its
previous location like gets done for the Wizard if you return to his
level before he comes to you.  And objects would need to carry along a
lot more information so that they could be given back to current owner
or be put back into container when you return to their level without
having wished for them.  One potential way around that is to put the
current owner, along with his inventory which includes the desired
artifact, onto the migrating monsters list; likewise, put the whole
enclosing container onto the list when the artifact is contained.
But I think this is liable to end being fairly fragile and overall not
worth the effort.


